      "content": "I understand you're in a rush, but to ensure you can handle this type of question in the exam, let's break it down quickly. The question asks for two examples of diction (word choice) from the sestet (lines 9-14) that show the speaker's realisation about his daughter. \n\nLooking at lines 9-14, can you pick out one word or phrase that describes the daughter's relationship with God or the divine?"
