      "content": "You are on the right track by noting that the speaker is making requests. To get both marks, we need to look at what he is *rejecting* versus what he is *requesting*. \n\nThink about the first stanza: he says 'do not bring me flowers' but then says 'Bring me... tears of dawns'. Why would he reject flowers, which are usually a symbol of celebration or welcome?"
